### Limitations the authors admit
- 2017ApJ...850..180J: Inclination-velocity degeneracy, beam smearing, ROTCUR errors underestimated
- 2019A&A...632A..61G: Models are axisymmetric and chi2 values are large
- 2021A&A...655A..25Z: Nuclear region barely resolved; higher resolution needed
- 2021A&A...655A..25Z: Cannot discriminate consecutive episodes from a decelerating wind
- 2024A&A...690A.169L: Small sample and large uncertainties preclude definitive conclusions on radial flows
- 2020Natur.581..269N: Unresolved JVLA only probes total molecular mass within ~15 kpc beam
- 2014A&A...567A.125G: Outflow rate is a lower limit due to limited velocity coverage
- 2014A&A...567A.125G: Resolution does not resolve kinematics of inner r~50 pc
- 2019ApJ...883..193N: Missing flux from lack of short baselines, so masses are lower limits
- 2019ApJ...883..193N: Residual is not a true chi2 because neighbouring pixels are correlated; modelling assumptions simple
- 2025NatAs...9.1553F: Magnification systematic uncertainty up to ~25%
- 2025NatAs...9.1553F: Clump number may increase with better data; ALMA beam larger than clumps so gas mass only for 7 clumps
- 2014A&A...565A..59D: Disk barely resolved so flux distribution and dynamical mass uncertain
- 2020MNRAS.493.3744F: FIR SED poorly sampled so L_IR and SFR are lower limits; kinematics unresolved; SLED has too few points
- 2025A&A...700A.285W: Torque method unvalidated by simulations, configuration likely unstable
- 2025A&A...700A.285W: Mass of young component is poorly constrained from single UV band; closed-box and alpha_CO assumptions
- 2015MNRAS.448.2224C: Upper limits depend on X_CO, which may be overestimated by up to an order of magnitude
- 2017ApJ...845..138S: Inclination derived from only two successful rings; real uncertainty may be much larger
- 2019A&A...621A..83S: Distance uncertain; warped or non-coplanar disks cannot be constrained; outer CO velocity field sparse
- 2020ApJ...892...68N: Tilted-ring uncertainties likely underestimated; distance systematics large
- 2025ApJ...992..211N: Distance uncertainty (69.3 vs 46.4 Mpc) gives ~30% systematic in MBH, dominant error
- 2020ApJ...889..162L: OH+ detection tentative (4 sigma); data insufficient to constrain all eight two-component parameters
- 2015ApJ...806L..34F: Sigma and Q depend strongly on assumed temperature and density; beam dilution up to factor 5
- 2017ApJ...843..136E: Missing short spacings: ~50% flux lost in CO(3-2); extended emission affected
- 2025MNRAS.536.3757A: Modest resolution may misclassify mergers as disks
- 2015Natur.522..455C: Dynamical masses very uncertain due to low spatial resolution
- 2021AN....342.1160P: Band 7 data not optimized for CO(3-2) and only partially covers the field/velocity range
- 2024A&A...684A..24P: Outflow marginally resolved; mass outflow rate may be a lower limit; Hbeta undetected
- 2019ApJ...871...85L: Stellar mass accurate only to ≲0.5 dex; possible AGN contamination
- 2019ApJ...871...85L: Outer rotation curve points limited by S/N
- 2019MNRAS.482.1499M: Low spatial resolution biases sigma_v and r1/2 high and Vrot low
- 2021A&A...656A..60A: Missing flux ~40-50% due to lack of single-dish data.
- 2021A&A...656A..60A: Mass model parameters are degenerate.
- 2025A&A...701A.113M: Observations cover only ~5 kpc, so DM density and scale length cannot be constrained simultaneously.
- 2020A&A...636A..37D: Large size uncertainties and sensitivity limits; spherical geometry underestimates density
- 2015ApJ...806...17R: Warm-gas mass per nucleus uses global Herschel ratio
- 2017ApJ...851..126V: Cycle 2 band 4 CO(3-2) data too noisy and unresolved, so cycle 3 data used
- 2024ApJ...968....9W: Marginal resolution, assumed T_dust, and uncertain inclination give large uncertainties in M_dyn and SFR
- 2015ApJ...812L..23S: alpha_CO uncertain; metallicity of ionised gas may not represent molecular gas; AGN cannot be excluded
- 2021A&A...652A..98G: Common T_dust adopted for all sources; mass estimates depend on assumed conversion factors
- 2021A&A...652A..98G: Spectral index maps only possible for 3 sources
- 2021A&A...652A..98G: Small-number statistics for orientation and correlations
- 2017MNRAS.465.4390B: Low resolution; size measurement uncertain, close to beam size
- 2017MNRAS.465.4390B: Results depend on assumed dust SED
- 2016ApJ...820L..39N: Higher-resolution data would be needed to confirm absence of substructure; dynamical mass is a lower limit
- 2020MNRAS.496.4061D: Keplerian rise not resolved; result depends on stellar mass model and Gamma
- 2020MNRAS.496.4061D: Low Gamma should be treated with caution; beam correlations neglected
- 2024PASA...41...76Z: Only line-of-sight velocity and CO traced mass are measured, so acceleration and central mass are underestimated
- 2020MNRAS.493.4294B: Uncertainty in C not included in M_dyn; CMB attenuation of [C II] not corrected; resolution does not resolve outflow regions
- 2015ApJ...811...39I: 150 pc resolution mixes AGN and SB contributions; CO(3-2) only partially covered
- 2019ApJ...884L..28I: Method does not correct for unknown intrinsic velocity dispersion; outflow and disk emission blended in the beam along the minor axis
- 2024A&A...685A.138V: Tdust poorly constrained; systematics dominate Mdust and Mstar
- 2015ApJ...811..124S: Systematic uncertainties in alpha_CO ~100% per method
- 2021ApJ...908..231M: Small and possibly biased sample
- 2021ApJ...908..231M: Surface density depends on alpha_CO choice
- 2019A&A...632A..33A: Missing flux from lack of short spacings; outflow mass uncertain by alpha_CO; outflow rate uncertain by a factor of a few; geometry unconstrained
- 2019A&A...632A..33A: Wings barely resolved
- 2020A&A...641A.151S: ALMA configuration resolves out diffuse gas; MRS 6.2 arcsec
- 2020A&A...641A.151S: Cannot exclude free-free contribution to continuum
- 2025MNRAS.541.2540Z: Circular-orbit assumption with mild non-circular motions; distance uncertainty (10%) not included in budget
- 2020A&A...637A..84P: Poor angular resolution prevents constraining Mdyn for most; thin-disc assumption too simple for some perturbed systems; MBH systematics up to ~0.4 dex
- 2014ApJ...797...90S: Mass estimates depend on uncertain X_CO; may be an order of magnitude lower if optically thin
- 2019ApJ...887...74F: Limited depth and resolution prevent distinguishing disk, merger and outflow
- 2019ApJ...887...74F: Dust mass depends strongly on the adopted kappa
- 2025A&A...699A.256P: Extended fraction is an upper limit dependent on noise and segmentation thresholds
- 2025A&A...699A.256P: Dust emission is low S/N so no radial dust profile
- 2013ApJ...770...13W: Source only marginally resolved; intrinsic size poorly constrained and inclination unknown
- 2013ApJ...770...13W: L_FIR uncertainties exclude dust temperature uncertainty
- 2018MNRAS.479.5440L: Velocity map very uncertain due to beam smearing and low S/N; Sigma not robust
- 2019MNRAS.489.1927S: Low spatial resolution prevents constraining geometry of the residual structure
- 2020ApJ...897..122L: Inclination unreliable for strong bars and solid-body-only velocity fields; bin covariance not accounted for
- 2025ApJ...988...72S: Large uncertainty on disk-wind angle due to assumptions on total velocity
- 2025ApJ...988...72S: Outer rotation curve uncertain
- 2025ApJ...988...72S: Milky Way alphaCO may be too high for RPS galaxies
- 2020ApJ...891...83C: Sizes and axial ratios poorly constrained due to limited resolution and beam elongation
- 2015A&A...580A...1M: Only one molecular line, so excitation mechanisms cannot be discriminated; X_CO uncertain
- 2015A&A...580A...1M: Jet orientation degenerate with lateral expansion velocity
- 2019A&A...628A.118B: Gas masses depend strongly on alpha_CO; large uncertainties on tau_dep and tau_SF
- 2024ApJ...972..111L: Only projected distances and radial velocities known; spatial offset of redshifted [C II] smaller than beam
