### 2021A&A...655A..25Z: The IBISCO survey. I. Multiphase discs and winds in the Seyfert galaxy Markarian 509 (2021; nearby_galaxies, agn_and_quasars; observational_alma_primary)
- question: What are the molecular gas content, disc kinematics, stability and molecular winds in the Seyfert 1.5 galaxy Mrk 509, and are the winds AGN- or SN-driven?
- step 3: Model disc kinematics
  - method: 3D tilted-ring fit; first run free inclination and PA, second run inclination fixed to 44 deg; residual cube, PV diagrams [4 Molecular Discs: "We fitted a 3D tilted-ring model to the emission line data-cube to provide a first order dynamical model of the CO-emitting gaseous disc."]
  - software: 3DBarolo
  - parameter: kinematic centre fixed to continuum position; PV slit 0.45 arcsec wide [4 Molecular Discs: "We fixed the kinematic center to the 1.2 mm continuum position"]
  - assumption: inclination 44 deg from GALEX UV imaging [4 Molecular Discs: "we fix it to 44 deg in the model"]
  - fitting: 3DBarolo tilted ring [Molecular Discs: "We fitted a 3D tilted-ring model to the emission line data-cube to provide a first order dynamical model of the CO-emitting gaseous disc."]
  - validation: second run residuals ~2% vs ~5% in first run in moment 0 [4 Molecular Discs: "The second run, with fixed inclination, produces residuals of amplitude about 2%, therefore we adopt the latter as best-fit disc model."]
- step 4: Dynamical mass and Toomre Q map
  - method: M_dyn = r v_rot^2/2G; Q_gas = a v_rot sigma/(pi R G Sigma_gas) pixel by pixel from moments 0 and 2 [6 Discussion: "The velocity dispersion and $\Sigma_{gas}$ are calculated pixel by pixel from the moment 2 and 0 maps, respectively; the radius $R$ is deprojected."]
  - parameter: a=1 up to R=1.1 arcsec, a=1.4 beyond [6 Discussion: "We adopt $a$=1 up to $R$=1.1 arcsec, where the rotation curve is steep, and $a$=1.4 at larger radii."]
  - validation: central 0.3 arcsec excluded for beam smearing [6 Discussion: "excluding the central region of 0.3 arcsec radius, to avoid the beam-smearing effect"]
- step 5: Molecular outflow properties
  - method: Residual cube spectra in regions A and B; Mdot=3 M v98/R; optically thin/thick alpha_CO; escape velocity; momentum load [5 Molecular Wind: "$$\dot{M}_{of} = 3 \frac{M_{of}\,v_{of}}{R_{of}}$$"]
  - software: 3DBarolo
  - assumption: alpha_CO = 0.3 (optically thin) and 0.8 (thick) Msun (K km/s pc^2)^-1 [5 Molecular Wind: "adopting a conversion factor $\alpha_{CO}\,= 0.3\mathrm{\,M_{\odot} (K\,km/s\,pc^{2})^{-1}}$ for the optically thin"]
  - validation: compare with momentum- and energy-conserving expectations and SN energetics [Discussion: "The molecular wind A and the ionised wind are consistent with a momentum conserving driving (black dashed line), and are well below the expectation for energy conserving winds."]
- step 6: Model nuclear warped disc
  - method: Nuclear disc fit with inclination 66 deg, PA 330 deg fixed; v_rot and dispersion free, first guesses 80 and 50 km/s [Inner disc model: "We allow two parameters to vary: the rotational velocity $v_{rot}$ and the velocity dispersion $\sigma_{gas}$ with first guess values set to 80 and 50 km/s"]
  - software: 3DBarolo
  - validation: compare model PV with data [Inner disc model: "The right panel of Fig.[5](#residuo0) shows the position velocity diagrams cut along the kinematic major axis (330 deg); where the grey-scale and blue contours refer to the data and the red contours to the model."]
- result: Disc PA = 248 ± 5 deg [4 Molecular Discs: "The disc model has a position angle PA = $248 \pm 5$ deg"]
- result: Dynamical mass = 2.0e10 ± 1.1e10 Msun [6 Discussion: "$M_{dyn}$ = (2.0 $\pm$ 1.1) $\times$ $10^{10}$ $\mathrm{M_{\odot}}$ within a $\sim$2.6 kpc radius"]
- result: Molecular gas fraction = ~5 ± not stated % [6 Discussion: "is then $\mu \sim 5 \%$"]
- result: Toomre Q_gas range = 0.5-10 ± not stated dimensionless [6 Discussion: "We find values that range from $Q_{gas}\approx$ 0.5 up to 10"]
- result: Outflow rate region A = 5.5-14.7 ± not stated Msun/yr [5 Molecular Wind: "$\dot{M}_{of}\,=\,5.5-14.7 \mathrm{\,M_{\odot}/yr}$"]
- result: Outflow rate region B = 0.86-2.30 ± not stated Msun/yr [5 Molecular Wind: "$\dot{M}_{of}\,=\,0.86-2.30 \mathrm{\,M_{\odot}/yr}$"]
- result: Total molecular outflow rate = 6.4-17.0 ± not stated Msun/yr [6 Discussion: "whose total molecular outflow rate is in the range 6.4 - 17.0 $\mathrm{M_\odot/yr}$"]
- result: Momentum load A = 0.5 ± 0.2 dimensionless [Table 3: "A | 250 | 0.3 | 0.51$\pm 0.05$ | 2.1-5.6 | 5.5-14.7 | 11-30 | 0.5 $\pm$ 0.2 | 140"]
- result: Star formation efficiency = 6.2e-9 ± not stated 1/yr [6 Discussion: "$SFE = SFR/M_{H_2} = 6.2 \times 10^{-9} \rm yr^{-1}$"]
- limitation (authors): Nuclear region barely resolved; higher resolution needed [4 Molecular Discs: "We note that observations with higher angular resolution would be required to better assess the kinematic properties in this region."]
- limitation (authors): Cannot discriminate consecutive episodes from a decelerating wind [5 Molecular Wind: "Current data cannot discriminate between these two scenarios."]
