### 2024A&A...690A.169L: Neutral atomic and molecular gas dynamics in the nearby spiral galaxies NGC 1512, NGC 4535, and NGC 7496 (2024; nearby_galaxies; multi_facility_alma_minor)
- question: Can H I kinematics constrain the disk orientation so as to improve CO and H I rotation curve determination, and what radial motions/mass flows do they show?
- step 1: Fit H I tilted rings
  - method: 3D tilted-ring fits in staged runs: free fit, fix center/Vsys, regularize geometry, fit Vrot and sigma [3.2: "Once the geometry of the galaxy is fixed, the kinematics are fitted."]
  - software: 3DBarolo
  - parameter: ring width 15 arcsec; weighting |cos θ|^2; rings with Vrot errors >±30 km/s dropped [3.2: "Rings that have large error bars ($>\SI{\pm30}{\kilo\meter\per\second}$) on the V$_{\text{rot}}$ values are neglected from here on."]
  - fitting: 3DBarolo default error calculation [3.2: "based on $^{\text{3D}}$Barolo’s default error calculation method"]
  - validation: Residual maps, scale height tests, comparison with literature [5.1: "we created residual maps by subtracting the modeled velocities from the observations"]
- step 2: Fit CO rotation curves
  - method: Start from H I best fit; fix center and Vsys; thin disk z0=100 pc; fit i, phi, Vrot, sigma then fix geometry [3.2: "After a first initial fitting stage where $i$, $\phi$, V$_{\text{rot}}$, and $\sigma_{\text{gas}}$ are kept free to vary, the geometry ($i$ and $\phi$) is fixed"]
  - software: 3DBarolo
  - validation: Compared to Lang et al. 2020 curves [4.2: "Overall the circular velocities derived by $^{\text{3D}}$Barolo agree well with the values from the previous work by (cite: 2020ApJ...897..122L)"]
- step 3: Radial velocities and mass flow rates
  - method: Fit Vrad with other parameters fixed, sin^2 φ weighting; Mdot=2πRΣHI Vrad ×1.33 for helium [3.4 Mass flow rates: "the H I mass flow $\dot{M}_{\text{HI}}$ is multiplied by the factor 1.33 which takes the primordial abundance of helium into account"]
  - software: 3DBarolo ELLPROF
  - assumption: Optically thin H I [3.4 Mass flow rates: "when assuming that the H I emission is optically thin"]
- result: NGC 1512 H I Vrot,max = 177.3 ± 16.4 km/s [Table 3: "$177.3\pm16.4$"]
- result: NGC 4535 H I Vrot,max = 188.8 ± 6.2 km/s [Table 3: "$188.8\pm6.2$"]
- result: NGC 7496 CO Vrot,max = 118.11 ± 6.09 km/s [Table 3: "$118.11\pm6.09$"]
- result: NGC 1512 average mass flow = 2.02 ± 1.85 Msun/yr [Table 2: "NGC 1512 | $0.75\pm0.75$ | $4.47\pm8.1$ | $2.02\pm1.85$"]
- limitation (authors): Small sample and large uncertainties preclude definitive conclusions on radial flows [5.4: "The limited sample size and the presence of substantial uncertainties in our data preclude us from making definitive conclusions."]
- not stated (card): ALMA project codes and PHANGS-ALMA data product version; 3DBarolo version and parameter file (ring separation, Bezier order, mask/normalization settings); Exact Bezier function parameters; H I cube processing details

