  - method: Thin exponential disk with constant (or arctan) rotation, constant dispersion, convolved with beam, MCMC fit to cube [Kinematic Analysis of the [C II] Emissi…: "we assume a [C II] line emission model in which the [C II] emission arises from a thin disk in which the emission exponentially declines"]
  - software: custom Python MCMC code (qubefit)
  - parameter: 9 or 10 free parameters [Kinematic Analysis of the [C II] Emissi…: "these 9 or 10 parameters uniquely determine the [C II] line emission in the model cube"]
  - assumption: Infinitely thin disk; thick disk tested [Kinematic Analysis of the [C II] Emissi…: "In the above models, we assume the [C II] emission arises from an infinitely thin disk."]
  - fitting: MCMC minimizing residuals; priors not stated [Kinematic Analysis of the [C II] Emissi…: "The program convolves the model cube with the observed beam and then minimizes the residuals between the convolved model and the observed data cube using a Markov Chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) approach"]
  - validation: Residuals below 3 sigma; compared with 3DBarolo (279 km/s) [Kinematic Analysis of the [C II] Emissi…: "which yields a rotational velocity of 279 km s$^{-1}$and a velocity dispersion of 72 km s$^{-1}$, consistent with our values"]
- step 4: Derive rotation curves, dynamical mass, Toomre Q
  - method: Mean-velocity and peak-velocity rotation curves; Mdyn = 2.32e5 v^2 R; Q averaged over R=3Rd [Dynamical Mass Estimate.: "$M_{\rm dyn}(R)$ = 2.32 $\times$ 10$^{5} v_{\rm rot}(R)^2 R$"]
  - parameter: R = 3 exponential scale lengths = 4.2 kpc [Dynamical Mass Estimate.: "we will assume the extent of the galaxy to be three times the exponential scale length of the modeled emission"]
  - assumption: Spherical mass distribution (30% uncertainty added) [Dynamical Mass Estimate.: "the mass distribution is implicitly assumed to be spherical"]
  - validation: Compared with FWHM-based v_rot of 300 +/- 50 km/s [Dynamical Mass Estimate.: "we get a rotational velocity of 300 $\pm$ 50 km s$^{-1}$"]
- result: Inclination-corrected rotational velocity = 272 ± +52/-13 km/s [main text: "an inclination-corrected rotational velocity of $v_{\rm rot}$ = 272$^{+52}_{-13}$ km s$^{-1}$"]
- result: Position angle = 105.2 ± 1.7 deg [main text: "position angle of 105.2 $\pm$ 1.7$^{\rm o}$"]
- result: Inclination = 42 ± +3/-8 deg [main text: "an inclination angle of 42$^{+3}_{-8}$$^{\rm o}$"]
- result: Dynamical mass = 7.2e10 ± 2.3e10 Msun [Dynamical Mass Estimate.: "$M_{\rm dyn}$ = (7.2 $\pm$ 2.3) $\times$ 10$^{10} M_\odot$"]
- result: vrot/sigma_v = 3.4 ± +1.1/-0.3 dimensionless [main text: "Our estimate for $v_{\rm rot}/\sigma_v$ is 3.4$^{+1.1}_{-0.3}$"]
- result: Disk-averaged Toomre Q = 0.96 ± 0.30 dimensionless [Toomre-$Q$ Parameter.: "This yields $\bar{Q} = 0.96 \pm 0.30$ for DLA0817g."]
- limitation (authors): Unresolved JVLA only probes total molecular mass within ~15 kpc beam [main text: "the unresolved JVLA observations can only probe the total molecular mass within the beam of the JVLA observations"]
